WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.935
Here with me now is Secretary

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.303
of State Antony Blinken.

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:06.272
Thank you so much for joining me today.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.274
This march

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:12.212
within 120 miles of Moscow, Prigozhin

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:15.181
then abruptly stopped, turned around

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.850
yesterday afternoon.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.650
What happened?

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.685
Why

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.688
Dana, we don't

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.523
have full information, obviously,

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.090
and it's too soon

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:24.824
to tell exactly

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.059
where this is going to go.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.128
And I suspect that

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.162
this is a moving picture

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.231
and we haven't seen the last act yet.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.766
But we can say this.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:33.333
First of all,

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.801
what we've seen is extraordinary.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.469
And I think you've seen cracks

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.005
emerge that that weren't there before.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:42.008
First, in having Prigozhin raised

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.143
front and center

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.444
questioning the very premises

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.378
of the Russian aggression

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.781
against Ukraine to begin with.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.916
The argument that somehow Ukraine

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.885
or Naito posed a threat to Russia

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.421
and a direct challenge to Putin himself.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.458
So think about it this way.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.560
16 months ago,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.929
Russian forces were on the doorstep of

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.264
of Kiev, Ukraine,

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:05.465
thinking they were going to take the city

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:06.666
in a matter of days,

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.401
erase the country from the map.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.502
Now,

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.370
they had to be focused

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.371
on defending

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.239
Moscow, Russia's capital,

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.274
against mercenaries

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.975
of Putin's own making.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.978
So this raises lots of profound questions

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.313
that will be answered,

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.282
I think, in the days and weeks ahead.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:22.849
I understand

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.451
this is very much a moving

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.019
and a fluid situation.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.254
One thing that Senator Marco Rubio

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:28.922
said, he's,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:29.989
of course, a top Republican

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.391
on the Intelligence Committee.

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:31.925
He says that

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.460
top military officials

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.127
in Russia

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:34.961
may have been

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.362
replaced in order

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.731
to get Prigozhin to back down.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.801
Have any top military of many top

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.070
any top military officials, forgive me,

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.505
like the defense minister,

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.574
been ousted as far as the U.S. knows?

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.344
We we haven't seen that yet.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.445
But again,

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.614
I think we'll see this unroll further

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:55.682
in the days and weeks ahead.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:55.915
There's

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:59.018
no secret to the fact that Prigozhin was

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.920
very much a critic

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.122
of the

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.056
military leadership,

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.725
the minister of defense,

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.861
the head of the armed forces.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:11.264
So how this now unfolds in terms of

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:13.733
personnel,

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.302
all of that remains to be seen.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.036
We are intensely

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:19.239
focused on on Ukraine and making sure

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.173
that Ukraine continues

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:22.308
to have what it needs to defend itself

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.610
to take back the territory

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.110
that the Russians

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.312
have seized over the past 16 months.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.780
And we're very focused

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.448
on maintaining

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.183
the unity of purpose in action

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.217
that has been a hallmark

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.252
of Ukraine's success to date.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.853
The president brought together

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.054
not only the national security

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.723
cabinet yesterday,

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.158
but brought together leaders

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.293
from among our key allies and partners.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.761
He instructed the rest of us

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.929
to fan out, to engage

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:43.963
all of our allies and partners,

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.565
to make sure we were closely

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:46.900
coordinating and keeping the focus

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.300
where it needs

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:47.800
to be

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:48.768
on Ukraine,

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:49.402
on the efforts

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.503
that they're making to take back

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:51.404
the territory that

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:52.205
Russia has taken from that.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:54.107
I understand that.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:54.607
But just a

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:57.110
saying on Vladimir Putin for a minute.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:58.411
Do you believe that

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.746
this is the beginning of the end

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.681
for Vladimir Putin?

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:03.383
I don't want to speculate about that.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:03.983
This is,

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.251
first of all,

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.953
an internal matter for Russia.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.022
What we've seen is this, though.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.290
We've seen this aggression

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.791
against Ukraine

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.027
become a strategic failure

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.361
across the board.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.696
Russia is weaker

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.531
economically, militarily.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.399
Its standing around

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:20.667
the world has plummeted.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:21.267
It's managed

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.369
to get Europeans off of Russian energy.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:25.305
It's managed to unite

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:26.239
and strengthen NATO's

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.307
with with new members

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.575
and a stronger alliance.

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.344
It's managed to alienate from Russia

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.213
and unite together Ukraine in ways

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.847
that it's never been before.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.449
This is just an added

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:36.916
chapter

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.851
to a very, very bad book

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.787
that Putin has written for Russia.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.622
But what's so striking about it

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:43.923
is it's internal

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.593
The fact that you have from within

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.460
someone directly

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.995
questioning Putin's authority,

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.630
directly questioning the premises

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.631
that upon

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.333
which he launched this aggression

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:54.434
against Ukraine,

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.903
that in and of itself is something very,

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:57.971
very powerful.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.839
It adds cracks

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.941
where those go when they get there.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.676
Too soon to say

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.378
But it clearly raises new questions

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:06.379
that Putin has to deal with.

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:08.982
You talked about Ukraine.

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:09.482
Of course,

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.283
Ukraine

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.885
did launch simultaneous counteroffensive

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.555
against several Russian fronts

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:17.724
while all of this was happening.

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:19.025
What is your understanding

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.094
of the latest on the ground in Ukraine?

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:21.494
And will

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.463
they be able to take advantage

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.231
of the chaos on the battlefield?

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.734
How much is the U.S. and U.S.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:28.368
allies?

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:28.801
NATO's

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.737
leaning into the chaos

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:33.273
in order to take advantage

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.274
So these are early days

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.475
for the counteroffensive.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.443
It's going to play out over weeks,

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.445
maybe even over months.

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:41.247
The Ukrainians have in hand what they

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.782
what they need to be successful

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:43.816
It's challenging.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.184
It's a it's a tough terrain.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.286
The Russians have put in place

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:47.687
lots of defenses

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:48.988
over the last months

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:49.822
in anticipation

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:50.823
of this counter-offensive.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.458
But it is progressing

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:53.092
and to the extent

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.261
that Russia is now distracted,

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.462
that Putin has to worry

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.398
about what's going on inside of Russia

00:04:58.398 --> 00:04:59.766
as much as he has to worry about

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:01.601
what he's trying to do.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.770
Not successfully in Ukraine.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.138
I think that creates

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.105
an additional advantage

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.440
for the Ukrainians to take advantage of.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.975
But regardless,

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.176
they are pressing forward.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.778
They have a clear plan.

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:12.979
They're pursuing it.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:15.214
Well, and the Ukrainian foreign minister,

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.684
I know you heard this, he says it's time

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.452
for the US and others

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.354
to put a foot on the gas,

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:22.622
give Ukraine everything

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.090
it needs to finish this.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.525
Is that going to happen?

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.093
Well, I spoke to my

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.494
my friend and counterpart, Dmitry Kelly,

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.829
but just yesterday

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.898
we speak we speak pretty regularly

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.299
and throughout

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:34.300
we have worked to make sure

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.535
that the Ukrainians have what they need,

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:36.469
when they need it

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.371
to do as well as they possibly can

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:40.173
on the ground. We'll continue to do that.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:41.674
We're relentlessly focused on this.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.710
There's tremendous unity of purpose

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:45.211
and unity of action

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.412
among dozens of countries

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.548
that through the president's leadership,

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:50.116
we brought together and kept together.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:51.684
And we'll continue to do that.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.785
Secretary Blinken, Russia

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.354
has nearly 6000 nuclear

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:56.489
weapons, the largest stockpile

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:57.423
in the world.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.291
The situation

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.492
really revealed

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:00.893
that this very large

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:01.728
nuclear power

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:03.830
is facing some major instability.

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:05.298
Are you confident

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:07.734
that the nuclear weapons are secure?

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.001
And more broadly,

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:11.137
how concerned are you about

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.306
Russia being unstable right now?

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:15.875
Anytime you have

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:16.809
a major country

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:17.377
like Russia

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:20.480
that has signs of instability,

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:22.215
that's something of concern

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.015
and something that,

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:24.550
of course, we're very focused on

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.419
when it comes to their nuclear weapons.

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:29.222
We've seen no change in their posture

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:30.790
and we've made no change

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:31.858
in our own posture.

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:32.425
But it's something,

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:34.193
of course, we're looking at

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.862
very, very carefully.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:37.430
On Vladimir Putin

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.798
last year, the president said,

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:39.599
for God's sake,

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:42.835
this man cannot remain in power.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:45.071
Is that still the American position?

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:47.206
These are decisions

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:48.241
for the Russian people.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.643
And this entire chapter

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:53.179
is an internal matter.

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:55.915
It obviously has profound repercussions

00:06:56.783 --> 00:06:57.550
outside of Russia,

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.885
including potentially in Ukraine.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:06:59.685
But fundamentally,

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.354
this is a Russian matter.

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:02.321
It's not our business.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:03.823
It's not our purpose to choose

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:04.457
Russia's leaders.

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:06.559
That's up to the Russian people.

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:07.160
And we have

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.362
no no beef with the Russian people.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:12.932
On the contrary, What is one of the many,

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:14.267
many tragedies

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.968
of what Putin has done in Ukraine

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.737
is what it's done to the Russian people.

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:19.672
And you really have to ask,

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:21.741
how is this in any way

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:23.443
improve the lives of Russians?

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:24.177
Of course, it hasn't.

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:25.711
It's made them worse.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:26.679
But these are questions

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:27.280
that Russians

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.215
have to resolve for themselves.

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:30.683
I have to ask you about China.

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:33.085
You just went to Beijing last week.

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:34.554
It was an attempt to smooth,

00:07:34.554 --> 00:07:36.889
frayed relations with China.

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:38.224
Two days later,

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:39.392
President Biden calls

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:40.793
Xi Jinping a dictator,

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:41.894
which angered China

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:42.962
so much that they issued

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:44.530
an official diplomatic

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.665
reprimand to the U.S.

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:46.532
ambassador.

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:48.668
Was the president wrong to call Xi

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:49.802
Jinping a dictator?

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:52.138
Then it

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:52.872
is very

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:55.808
clear that when it comes to China,

00:07:57.143 --> 00:07:59.345
we are going to do

00:07:59.345 --> 00:08:01.247
and say things that they don't like,

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:03.182
they are going to do and say things

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:03.916
that we don't like.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:06.185
If you look at what comes out of

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:07.353
the Chinese foreign ministry

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:09.121
every day about the United States,

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.623
you'd hear plenty of that.

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.658
But the the purpose of the trip

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:14.727
at the president's instruction

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:17.263
was to try to bring a little bit

00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:19.232
more stability to the relationship

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:20.633
to demonstrate

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:21.200
that we're committed

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.702
to managing it responsibly,

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:24.504
which really is an obligation for us

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:25.204
and an expectation

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:26.806
that countries around the world have

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:28.908
and to be able to deal very directly

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:29.775
with our differences.

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.577
There's no secret about

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:32.478
about those differences.

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.247
There's no secret about

00:08:34.247 --> 00:08:36.249
concerns we have about democracy,

00:08:36.249 --> 00:08:37.483
about human rights,

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:38.551
about some of the actions

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:41.153
that China is taking around the world

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:44.090
and being able to have better, stronger,

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.691
sustained lines of communication means

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:46.926
we can talk about these differences

00:08:46.926 --> 00:08:47.960
directly.

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:50.096
We can work through them where

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:50.763
where we can,

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:52.164
but at the very least,

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:53.499
avoid misunderstandings,

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:54.600
avoid miscalculations.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.135
That's the fastest way

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:57.303
to go from the competition.

00:08:57.303 --> 00:08:59.305
We're in to a conflict we want to avoid.

00:08:59.305 --> 00:09:01.307
So I think on those terms,

00:09:01.674 --> 00:09:03.776
the visit was was positive.

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:04.510
And again,

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.112
one of the things I told the Chinese is

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:07.647
that we're going to continue

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:08.514
to do things

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:10.249
and to say things that you don't like,

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:11.017
do you?

00:09:11.017 --> 00:09:11.784
Just as you're to do

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:13.052
the same and we'll work through them.

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:13.920
Do you believe that Xi

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.054
Jinping is a dictator?

00:09:16.289 --> 00:09:18.291
The president speaks clearly.

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:19.926
He speaks candidly.

00:09:19.926 --> 00:09:20.459
I've worked for him

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:21.894
for more than 20 years

00:09:21.894 --> 00:09:23.663
and he speaks for all of us.

00:09:23.663 --> 00:09:24.297
Okay.

00:09:24.297 --> 00:09:25.831
Secretary of State

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:26.632
Antony Blinken

00:09:26.632 --> 00:09:28.100
thank you so much for joining us

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.969
this morning. Good to be with you, Don.

